NATIVE DISPLAY REPAIR PREREQUISITES

These are uninstalled development sources, required together with
fred.workspaces 2.0.11. They do not select a candidate or authorize a native
installation. Keep the existing DPMS, idle-inhibit and connector guards.

  Source: Hyprland
  <https://github.com/greenermoose/Hyprland/tree/develop/plan54-output-workspace-logging>
  Base: v0.56.2-fred.3
  Development head: 3b1b3f15

  Source: Aquamarine
  <https://github.com/greenermoose/aquamarine/tree/develop/plan54-commit-attribution>
  Base: v0.15.1-fred.1
  Development head: 25f5e5d

The forks are the source of truth. The adjacent source-only patches reproduce
these changes on their carried package bases. DisplayLog.hpp is an exact copy
of the tested native sink; a regression checks that the patch embeds that same
header. Export the patches into the native package registry and frozen recipes
during candidate preparation; do not install a checkout or replace the
existing package pin without that procedure.


WORKSPACE ACTION

hl.dsp.workspace.select({workspace="5", monitor="DP-1"}) returns the usual
native dispatcher result table. It accepts normal numeric workspace IDs 1–160
and an exact existing output name. It creates/assigns that workspace before
activating it. A side output uses changeWorkspace with no mouse movement and
no focus change; that path also leaves held mouse buttons alone. Moving the
focused output's currently active workspace away is rejected. There is no
focus-and-restore fallback. Output loss is a failure, not proof of physical
completion. Native workspace-selected events record the observed input-output
preservation result. The exported CLogger data layout stays unchanged for
existing native plugins.

Retire this local action when upstream provides equivalent bounded,
output-targeted activation without borrowing focus or moving the pointer.


NATIVE LOGGING

Warnings/errors from the compositor and the actual Aquamarine callback use one
emission sink. A small allowlist also retains connector transitions, output
disable and modeset events. Frame, cursor, input and other debug/trace records
do not enter this production sink. Existing verbose logging controls and the
original Hyprland file retain their separate native behavior.

Each bounded single-line payload contains wall-clock and CLOCK_MONOTONIC
nanoseconds, component, numeric syslog severity and PID. Clock samples are
emission-time observations, not claims of nanosecond hardware accuracy. The
journal stream consumes <priority> prefixes. The same payload is appended to
display.log in the compositor instance directory and flushed immediately. This
makes it visible to readers; it is not an fsync guarantee. File open rejects
symlinks/nonregular files, and sink failure reports to stderr.

Synchronous commit records add output, CRTC, connector status, in-flight state
and test flag at the emitting site. Terminal commit failures also record
relevant commit properties. Asynchronous worker failures carry output, CRTC,
commit ID and errno in both result-drain paths. crtc=0 or an unknown output
means the identity was unavailable. Unsupported async capabilities and
cancellation remain their existing control paths, not synthetic GPU failures.
No frame scheduling, cancellation or recovery decisions were changed.

Retire the native logging changes when upstream provides equivalent
attribution, emission clocks, filtering and prompt journal/file visibility.


VERIFICATION

Run the isolated product regressions from the product root:

    python3 -B -m unittest discover -s desktop/tests -p 'test_workspace_*.py' -q
    python3 -B -m unittest discover -s desktop/tests -p test_native_display_logging.py -q
    python3 -B -m unittest discover -s desktop/tests -p test_compositor.py -q
    python3 -B -m unittest discover -s desktop/plugins/fred.workspaces/tests -q
    desktop/widget-proof fred.workspaces

The native proof is desktop/proofs/native-display-logging.cpp. Build it with
C++23, the matching Aquamarine private logger header, pixman/libdrm include
flags, and the rebuilt aquamarine plus hyprutils libraries. It instantiates
the actual Aquamarine logger and this exact sink, never a backend, DRM device
or compositor. All error records are explicitly synthetic. Run with a new
scratch file; optionally route through systemd-cat --level-prefix=yes under a
distinct proof identifier. Check file visibility before logger destruction,
identical file/journal payloads, priorities 3,3,3,6,4, debug filtering, line
bounds and the 20 ms emission gap. Never mistake those errors for an incident.

On 2026-11-11 the rebuilt Aquamarine library and its fake-backend attachments,
output and commitThread tests pass. The real-window test was not run. The
complete Hyprland 0.56.2-4.2 package now builds and links; its version-only
entry runs with the staged Aquamarine library. Aquamarine 0.15.1-1.2 builds as
a package. Frozen recipes and archive verification live in tamlinux-packages.
The final synthetic proof passes its file/priority/envelope checks. Journal
stream envelope timestamps are not exact per-line emission times: one observed
delta was approximately −2 microseconds. Use the payload monotonic clock for
emission ordering; never derive one from an old untimed log.

Before physical acceptance, require the paired native/user-package integration
receipt, exact candidate Test authority, actual candidate service/helper
journal routing, quiet idle and the approved Dell continuity matrix. A native
installation and any necessary logout/login retain their individual approval
and rollback requirements.
